<section id="fog">
<h2><span class="n">10</span>Flow visualization: laminar fog generator</h2>
<p>To make the flow visible I built a fog generator that feeds streaklines into the tunnel inlet. It is a 6 in acrylic cylinder about 9 in tall. An ultrasonic mister sits under about 2 in (800 mL) of water, and a 4.5 in headspace above it lets the fog settle before it leaves. A 1/4 in valve at the outlet feeds four ports.</p>
<p>Because the tunnel runs on suction, the inlet sits slightly below room pressure. That difference draws fog through the generator, so no separate blower is needed. A needle valve limits the draw so the water surface stays calm. The 1/4 in valve is the smallest flow area in the line, so adding ports would only dilute each streak. I kept four.</p>
